    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43991" root="&#xA;                        نصى&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاصِيَةٌ</span></b> 
                         properly, in the language of the [classical] Arabs, The <i>place where the hair grows in
the fore part of the head:</i> and hence, the <i>hair
of that part;</i> the <i>hair over the forehead;</i> (Az,
TA;) [and this is the general meaning;) <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُصَّةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُرَّةٌ</span>. (Msb, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قص</span>.) The <i>forelock</i>
of a horse. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاصِيَةُ بَنِى فُلاَنٍ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَذَرَّى</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذِرْوَةٌ</span>.

